---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="AI Design Repository | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="How I built, and still own, shared AI design repos that hundreds of designers, PMs, and engineers use across Microsoft teams."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--blue">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="container case-hero__grid">
        <div class="case-hero__main">
        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back"><span class="back-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Back to selected projects</span></a>
        <h1>I build the repos our teams use to design with AI</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Our designers were prototyping in Figma and their own separate repos, and nobody could build on anyone else's work. I proposed one shared repo, built it, and still own it. It's now required for designers across multiple teams, and PMs and engineers work in it too. I've since built several more, and hundreds of people use them.
        </p>

        <div class="outcomes-strip" aria-label="Project outcomes">
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Hundreds</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Designers, PMs, and engineers using the repos I've built</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Required</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">The standard way our designers prototype</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Active</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Used for ideation, demos, customer concepts, and handoff</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="glance-card" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
          <h2 id="glance-title">At a glance</h2>
          <dl class="glance">
              <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Senior Content Designer</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Ownership</dt><dd>I proposed it, built it, and own the architecture and roadmap</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Collaboration</dt><dd>My design manager, designers, PMs, and engineers</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>The prototyping workflow for multiple teams</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Required for designers. Engineering handoff is in progress.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Internal use. Diagrams redrawn with generic labels.</dd></div>
            </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="container case-shell">
        <aside class="disclosure" aria-label="Project disclosure">
          <strong>About the evidence</strong>
          <p>This is internal Microsoft work. I redrew the diagrams with generic labels and left out anything that isn't public.</p>
        </aside>

        <nav class="case-toc" aria-label="AI design repository case study sections">
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#problem">The problem</a></li>
            <li><a href="#decision">The decision</a></li>
            <li><a href="#architecture">How it connects</a></li>
            <li><a href="#operating-model">How people contribute</a></li>
            <li><a href="#outcome">What changed</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reflection">What I learned</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <section id="problem" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>The problem</h2>
          <p>Designers were prototyping in Figma and their own separate repos. Each one worked fine on its own. But every new idea started from scratch, and nobody could pick up someone else's prototype and keep going.</p>
          <p>There were no rules for how to structure a repo, contribute, review, or check quality. We had plenty of prototypes and nothing that added up.</p>
          <p>I wanted one place where the work could build on itself.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="ownership-title">
          <h2 id="ownership-title">My role</h2>
          <p>I tested the idea with a few experiments, then proposed the repo and built it myself. I worked with my design manager on requirements, and we set the roadmap together.</p>
          <p>I made most of the architecture and implementation calls. When an internal tool already did part of the job well, I plugged it in instead of rebuilding it.</p>
          <p>I still own the repo: the architecture, how people contribute, the quality checks, and the roadmap.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="decision" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>One required repo, not another optional tool</h2>
          <p>The main call was to put all of the team's prototyping in one governed repo instead of adding another optional tool.</p>
          <p>That meant deciding a lot more than folder names. I designed:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The folder structure</li>
            <li>The branching model</li>
            <li>Pull requests and approvals</li>
            <li>How designers contribute and update shared work</li>
            <li>How the repo gets distributed and maintained</li>
            <li>Which internal tools to integrate rather than rebuild</li>
            <li>How prototypes move toward engineering handoff</li>
            <li>Which automated checks protect quality</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Now designers build on each other's work instead of redoing it, and PMs and engineers work in the same place.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="workflow-caption">
          <div class="workflow-compare" role="img" aria-label="Before and after workflow comparison showing fragmented individual tools replaced by one shared governed repository">
            <section class="workflow-panel workflow-panel--before">
              <span class="diagram-label">Before</span>
              <h3>Fragmented prototypes</h3>
              <div class="tool-row" aria-hidden="true"><span>Figma</span><span>Separate repos</span></div>
              <ul>
                <li>Isolated work</li>
                <li>Repeated setup</li>
                <li>Limited reuse</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
            <div class="workflow-shift" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <section class="workflow-panel workflow-panel--after">
              <span class="diagram-label">After</span>
              <h3>Shared repository</h3>
              <div class="tool-row" aria-hidden="true"><span>Reuse</span><span>Review</span><span>Checks</span></div>
              <ul>
                <li>Team contributions</li>
                <li>Shared foundations</li>
                <li>Demos and handoff</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="workflow-caption">
            <strong>From scattered prototypes to one repo.</strong> Shared work, reviews, checks, demos, and handoff all live in one place.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="architecture" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>How it connects</h2>
          <p>The repo doesn't try to do everything itself. It holds our shared context and rules, and connects to the MCPs, agents, knowledge bases, repos, and internal tools we already had.</p>
          <p>You start with a design or product goal. The repo applies our guidance, pulls in the right tools, and produces a prototype or reusable piece of design. Then it goes through review, evals, and handoff.</p>
          <p>I'm using generic names because the internal systems aren't public.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="architecture-caption">
          <ol class="system-flow">
            <li><span>1</span><strong>Product goal</strong><small>Design request or idea</small></li>
            <li><span>2</span><strong>Shared repository</strong><small>Context, rules, and reusable foundations</small></li>
            <li><span>3</span><strong>Connected capabilities</strong><small>MCPs, agents, knowledge bases, and tools</small></li>
            <li><span>4</span><strong>Design output</strong><small>Prototype or reusable experience</small></li>
            <li><span>5</span><strong>Review and handoff</strong><small>Evaluation, decisions, and engineering inputs</small></li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption id="architecture-caption">
            <strong>Simplified system view.</strong> Internal names are removed.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="operating-model" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>How people contribute</h2>
          <p>A whole team can only rely on a repo if there's a clear way to change it. So I set up how people use it, change it, and trust it.</p>
          <p>Contributors work in branches and open pull requests. Approvals protect shared work. Automated checks cover:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Evaluations</li>
            <li>Design-token compliance</li>
            <li>Content quality</li>
            <li>Accessibility</li>
          </ul>
          <p>An AI prototype that renders isn't automatically good. The checks hold it to the same bar as the rest of our design work.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="operating-caption">
          <ol class="operating-flow">
            <li><span>01</span><strong>Create a branch</strong><small>Start from the shared foundation</small></li>
            <li><span>02</span><strong>Propose a change</strong><small>Build or update reusable work</small></li>
            <li><span>03</span><strong>Run checks</strong><small>Evaluate tokens, content, and accessibility</small></li>
            <li><span>04</span><strong>Review and approve</strong><small>Protect the shared system</small></li>
            <li><span>05</span><strong>Merge and reuse</strong><small>Make approved work available to the team</small></li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption id="operating-caption">
            <strong>How a change gets in.</strong> Branches, checks, and reviews keep shared work from turning into throwaway work.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="training-title">
          <h2 id="training-title">Getting the team ready</h2>
          <p>Designers had to work differently, too. Before the wider release, I trained the team on VS Code, GitHub, GitHub Copilot, branches, and pull requests.</p>
          <p>That's what made the switch work. I didn't just hand people a repo and tell them to use it. They'd already picked up the basics before anyone asked them to contribute.</p>
          <p>This was part of a bigger AI training effort across the design org, which I cover in <a href={`${base}/work/org-ai-initiatives`}>its own case study</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="outcome" class="content-section">
          <div class="reading-column">
            <h2>What changed</h2>
            <p>After months of iteration, I released it to designers, PMs, and engineers across multiple teams. It's now required for designers and a core part of how the group develops and shows ideas. I've built several more design repos since, and together they're used by hundreds of people.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="impact-grid" aria-label="Current repository uses">
            <div><strong>Design and ideation</strong><span>Shared prototypes and reusable work</span></div>
            <div><strong>Demos and customers</strong><span>Leadership reviews and customer concepts</span></div>
            <div><strong>Engineering handoff</strong><span>Components, Storybook, versions, guided runs, and backlog inputs</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="reading-column">
            <p>I don't have a speed number to share. What changed is that the work adds up now. People extend what's already there instead of starting over with every idea.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="handoff-title">
          <h2 id="handoff-title">What's next: engineering handoff</h2>
          <p>Right now I'm working on getting prototype decisions into development more cleanly. Designers and engineers are trying out reusable components, Storybook, versions, guided runs, and more structured backlog items that come straight from the repo.</p>
          <p>This is still in progress. The repo fixed the scattered-prototype problem. Once more people used it, the next gap was obvious: the path from design to engineering.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="reflection" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What I learned</h2>
          <p>I think the biggest lesson is that adoption starts before launch. The structure, the contribution process, the checks, and the training all mattered because they gave people a reliable way to take part. Building the repo was only part of the work.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="next-system" aria-labelledby="next-system-title">
          <div>
            <h2 id="next-system-title">Still growing</h2>
            <p>The repo keeps changing with the teams that use it. Next up is turning shared prototypes into cleaner inputs for engineering.</p>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <hr class="divider" />
        <nav class="case-pagination" aria-label="Case study navigation">
          <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="case-pagination__link">
            <span class="case-pagination__icon case-pagination__icon--index" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Project index</span><span class="case-pagination__title">All selected projects</span></span>
          </a>
          <a href={`${base}/work/hackathon`} class="case-pagination__link case-pagination__link--next">
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Next project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Hackathon PM agent</span></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: 0; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede { max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-12); font-size: var(--size-xl); line-height: 1.6; }
  .outcome { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .outcome__label { max-width: 25ch; font-size: var(--size-sm); color: var(--muted); }
  .case-shell { max-width: calc(var(--narrow) + 6rem); }
  .reading-column { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin-inline: auto; }
  .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .content-section h2, .case-summary h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .content-section:not(:first-child) h2 { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  .content-section p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .content-section ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6) var(--space-6); }
  .content-section li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }

  .disclosure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: 0 auto var(--space-12); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-blue-soft); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  .disclosure strong { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: none; }
  .disclosure p { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }

  .case-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .case-meta dt { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .case-meta dd { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .case-toc { max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-16); padding-block: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .case-toc__label { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: none; }
  .case-toc ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .case-toc li { --toc-divider: var(--border); display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .case-toc li + li { margin-left: var(--space-4); }
  .case-toc li + li::before { content: ''; width: 2px; height: 16px; margin-right: var(--space-4); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--toc-divider); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n + 1) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 32px; align-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.3; text-decoration: none; }
  .case-toc a:hover { color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 5px; }

  .evidence-figure { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-12) auto var(--space-16); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption { width: 100%; margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }

  .workflow-compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-3); align-items: stretch; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; }
  .workflow-panel { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .workflow-panel--before { background: var(--surface-tint); }
  .workflow-panel h3 { margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .workflow-panel ul { margin-left: var(--space-4); }
  .workflow-panel li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .diagram-label { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .tool-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .tool-row span { padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #fff; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .workflow-shift { display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-blue); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; }

  .system-flow, .operating-flow { --flow-gap: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--flow-gap); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); list-style: none; }
  .system-flow li, .operating-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 185px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .system-flow li::after, .operating-flow li::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 100%; z-index: 1; width: var(--flow-gap); height: 2px; background: var(--portfolio-blue); transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .system-flow li::before, .operating-flow li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 50%; left: calc(100% + var(--flow-gap) - 9px); z-index: 2; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-top: 2px solid var(--portfolio-blue); border-right: 2px solid var(--portfolio-blue); transform: translateY(-50%) rotate(45deg); }
  .system-flow li:last-child::after, .system-flow li:last-child::before, .operating-flow li:last-child::after, .operating-flow li:last-child::before { content: none; }
  .system-flow li > span, .operating-flow li > span { display: grid; width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .system-flow strong, .operating-flow strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .system-flow small, .operating-flow small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .operating-flow { border-color: #e1c35f; background: var(--surface-tint); }

  .impact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-8) auto; }
  .impact-grid div { display: flex; min-height: 150px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .impact-grid strong { color: var(--portfolio-blue); line-height: 1.35; }
  .impact-grid span { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); line-height: 1.5; }

  .next-system { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-16) auto 0; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .next-system .tag { color: var(--portfolio-yellow); }
  .next-system h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: #fff; }
  .next-system p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); }
  .divider { margin-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-8); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .case-toc ul { gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .case-toc li + li { margin-left: 0; }
    .case-toc li + li::before { content: none; }
    .system-flow, .operating-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .system-flow li, .operating-flow li { min-height: 150px; }
    .system-flow li::after, .operating-flow li::after { top: 100%; left: 50%; width: 2px; height: var(--flow-gap); transform: translateX(-50%); }
    .system-flow li::before, .operating-flow li::before { top: calc(100% + var(--flow-gap) - 9px); left: 50%; border-top: 0; border-right: 2px solid var(--portfolio-blue); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--portfolio-blue); transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(45deg); }
    .impact-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .impact-grid div { min-height: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 130px; }
    .disclosure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-12); padding-block: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-6); }
    .case-toc a { min-height: 44px; }
    .workflow-compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .workflow-shift { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .system-flow, .operating-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .system-flow li, .operating-flow li { min-height: auto; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .outcome:hover,
    .case-meta div:hover,
    .workflow-panel:hover,
    .system-flow li:hover,
    .operating-flow li:hover,
    .impact-grid div:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  /* ---- Visual refresh: open diagrams, no boxes inside boxes ---- */
  .workflow-compare { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 48px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); align-items: center; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; }
  .workflow-panel { height: 100%; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; box-shadow: var(--elev-1); }
  .workflow-panel--before { background: #fff; box-shadow: none; }
  .workflow-panel--after { border-color: rgba(17,85,204,0.35); box-shadow: var(--elev-2); }
  .diagram-label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; height: 24px; padding: 0 0.6rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface-tint); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .workflow-panel--after .diagram-label { background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; }
  .workflow-panel h3 { margin-block: 0.75rem 0.75rem; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .workflow-panel ul { margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .workflow-panel li { position: relative; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; padding-left: 1.6rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .workflow-panel li::before { position: absolute; top: 0.1em; left: 0; display: grid; width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; }
  .workflow-panel--before li { color: var(--muted); }
  .workflow-panel--before li::before { content: '–'; background: #eef0f4; color: var(--muted); }
  .workflow-panel--after li::before { content: '✓'; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .tool-row { gap: 0.35rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .tool-row span { padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; background: #fff; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; }
